To minimize damage to the fields, I will divide the drones based on the current threat levels and the required number of drones for full protection. 

Field_1 has a threat level of 0.28 and requires 4 drones for full protection. Currently, it has 3 drones protecting it, and 1 drone is moving towards it, but we need at least one more drone to achieve full protection.

Field_2 is not currently being protected and has a low threat level (0.12), so it would be best to assign at least some drones there in case of an increase in threat.

Field_3 is being protected by 2 drones but requires 2 for full protection and has a very low threat level (0.01), making it a low priority. 

Field_4 has a low threat level (0.03) and currently has no protection. However, it requires 3 drones for full protection.

Given this information, I will prioritize sending available idle drones to fields needing protection, focusing on getting Field_1 fully protected first.

